Spelunky is the most mechanically tight and endlessly rewarding video game experience I've ever had. The skilled can complete the game in anywhere between 2-30 minutes, but more likely than not, you'll spend a fair amount of hours before you even see all the worlds the game has to offer (and possibly more than a hundred hours just to fully comprehend the game's myriad secrets). Randomized and difficult, though (practically) never unfair, the game never gets old and unlike so many titles I've played, progress is a result of skill and knowledge rather than grinding for higher stats or reading walkthroughs.
I could go on for ages about the sheer depth and brilliance of Spelunky (
), but truly, it's something you have to experience for yourself.

