The Quest is my favorite game of all. It is also my most played game, and I have played many single-player RPGs, including some that required around 200 hours to finish. It doesn't take very long to finish, but I played it dozens of times on other platforms and there are many interesting expansions.
I don't know what I can write to express how good I think this game is...
Let's just say
It's very well designed;
The replayability is phenomenal;
The graphics are superb (Just my humble opinion. Almost everything looks sharp and full of detail on my laptop's relatively large screen, except for a few small things like shop signs, but it's almost certain that Redshift can create a game with even better graphics everywhere, so stay tuned);
There are many neat functions you may use or ignore - it's up to you;
Many choices that affect how NPCs regard you, and I assure you that those features are very well implemented.
It's very awesome! :D

As far as point and click adventures go, Deponia is (to me) on par with the Monkey Island series. It contains:
a) a character that you'll fall in love with;
b) lots of funny dialogue and even hilarious cutscenes;
c) totally unlogical puzzles, untill you solved them (and then they do seem logical! q-: )
A must-have for even the most basic point-and-click-adventure fan!

I played on Wargame EE for years, and I enjoyed it a lot;
Well, this game is a whole new level of details and awareness, good work.
Moreover, almost 2000 units is a really impressive amount.
Some criticism though :
- Improve AI on its intelligence (althought it's satisfying enough currently);
- Modify the AI behaviour on sea battles, it's just unfunny to play against something so aggressive;
- The more units you would add to the game (Leclerc 140 mm GIAT ftw), the most pleased we would be.
Thank you for reading.

